        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          <p class="text-blue-50">
            <strong class="text-white"
              >I've experienced the pricing problem firsthand.</strong
            >
            After successfully building and selling AnciCare to CorVel Corporation
            (NYSE: CVL) in 2002, I was shocked when I needed an MRI for myself years
            later. Hospitals quoted <span class="text-red-300 font-bold"
              >$8,000</span
            >, but my insurance would only pay their negotiated rate of <span
              class="text-yellow-300 font-bold">$1,600</span
            >
            — which became my responsibility because I hadn't met my deductible.
          </p>

          <p class="text-blue-50">
            The games hospitals play frustrated me most. <strong
              class="text-white"
            >
              If you mention insurance, they won't offer cash prices. But
              approach them without mentioning insurance, and suddenly cash
              discounts become available.</strong
            > These manipulative practices hurt the
            <span class="text-[#cc9933] font-bold">90+ million Americans</span> who
            are uninsured or underinsured.
          </p>

          <p class="text-blue-50">
            That's when I realized: <strong class="text-white"
              >I had already solved this problem.</strong
            >
            Through AnciCare (1994-2002), we had proven that transparent, fair pricing
            works at scale. We had served 400,000+ patients, delivered $400M+ in
            savings, and built such a valuable business that
            <strong class="text-[#cc9933]"
              >CorVel Corporation (NYSE: CVL) acquired us</strong
            >—and they're
            <strong class="text-[#cc9933]"
              >still operating our model 20+ years later.</strong
            >
          </p>

          <div class="bg-white/10 rounded-2xl p-6 mt-8">
